# UEQ-S – Adjective Reference



These definitions are for the researcher's internal reference during
playtesting and analysis, not explanations to participants.

## Pragmatic Quality
Focus: Usability, clarity, and task efficiency.

| Adjective pair | Meaning | Example in ASCIIA BAY |

+ Obstructive (aufdringlich) – Supportive
Feedback interrupts progress unnecessarily vs. helps with crafting.

+ Complicated – Easy 
Players struggle with several controls vs. interact easily.

+ Inefficient – Efficient 
Feedback takes effort without clear benefit vs. improves crafting efficiently. 

+ Confusing – Clear 
Players cannot tell what preferences do vs. understand their effects. 

## Hedonic Quality
Focus: Stimulation, originality, and interest.

| Adjective pair | Meaning | Example in ASCIIA BAY |

+ Boring – Exciting 
Feedback feels tedious vs. creates excitement about crafting. |

+ Not interesting – Interesting 
Players ignore the feature vs. want to explore its possibilities.

+ Conventional – Inventive 
Familiar rating controls vs. an unusually creative feedback interaction. |

+ Usual – Leading edge 
Feels like a typical interface vs. a novel approach to AI crafting. |
